Usage: ai-cockpit verify [OPTIONS] --repo <REPO>

Options:
      --repo <REPO>
          
      --work-item <WORK_ITEM>
          
      --command <COMMAND>
          
      --args <ARGS>
          
      --workers <WORKERS>
          Maximum worker count. Work Item verification defaults to serial and rejects parallel requests until per-node dependencies and outputs can be verified by the Runtime [default: 1]
      --stage <STAGE>
          [default: task]
      --timeout-seconds <TIMEOUT_SECONDS>
          Finite command timeout in seconds. Explicit values require a finite Contract or repository policy ceiling; omission defaults to 600 seconds for Cargo package tests and 300 seconds otherwise
      --plan-only
          Resolve the route and emit its deterministic verification plan without spawning project verification commands
      --base-revision <BASE_REVISION>
          Required for pr/merge/release when no Work Item Contract supplies the immutable base revision
      --archived-recovery
          Run one fresh, current-Runtime verification for an archived Work Item and append a source-integration recovery receipt
  -h, --help
          Print help
